    {
      "@id": "x:doc",
      "@type": "Container"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To investigate factors predictive of future lupus nephritis development when systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) is diagnosed.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "In particular, a low AGR (aHR 4.972, 95% CI: 2.394 – 10.326, p < 0.001) was strongly associated with an increased risk of future lupus nephritis development.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n2",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Young age, low C3, high anti-dsDNA titre and presence of anti-Sm antibody at diagnosis of SLE were associated with a risk of future lupus nephritis",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n3",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Notably, the factor associated with the greatest hazard for lupus nephritis was a low AGR (aHR 4.972, 95% CI: 2.394 – 10.326, p < 0.001).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n4",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "AGR, with the highest AUC, had the highest discrimination ability for development of lupus nephritis among the three variables.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n5",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Thus, the cumulative incidence of lupus nephritis was 34.8% (136 of 391)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n6",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "one possible explanation is that a low AGR, indicating a greater proportion of globulin relative to total protein, reflects the higher amounts of antibodies in the serum of patients with SLE.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n7",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Based on the aHR, we estimated that risk of developing lupus nephritis increased by 4% per 100 IU/ml increase of anti-dsDNA titre.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n8",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "First, this study was retrospective in design, and was a single center study in Korea. Thus further studies are required with larger number of subjects from different ethnic populations to confirm the present results.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n9",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Of 278 patients newly diagnosed with SLE during the study period but without lupus nephritis at that time, 241 did not and 37 did develop nephritis on follow-up. The median follow-up duration was 44.9 (range: 29.0 – 68.4) months.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n10",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The median time to development of lupus nephritis was 30.1 (range: 16.2 – 54.7) months.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n11",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "At initial diagnosis of SLE, patients who developed lupus nephritis during follow-up were significantly younger [28.4 (± 9.7) years vs. 40.8 (± 14.4) years, p < 0.001] and had a lower serum albumin level [3.24 (± 0.62) g/dl vs. 3.86 (± 0.54) g/dl, p < 0.00",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n12",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "On univariate analysis, factors significantly associated with an increased risk of developing lupus nephritis included younger age, lower AGR, lower C3, lower C4, higher anti-dsDNA titre and the presence of anti-Sm and anti-RNP antibodies (Table 2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n13",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "On multivariate analysis, the following factors remained significant: age [adjusted hazard ratio (aHR) 0.928, 95% confidence interval (CI): 0.895 – 0.961, p < 0.001], C3 (aHR 0.977, 95% CI: 0.966 – 0.989, p < 0.001), anti-dsDNA titre (aHR 1.004, 95% CI: 1.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n14",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The discrimination ability of the multivariable model was high (c index 0.898, 95% CI: 0.855 – 0.947).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n15",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The results of ROC analyses of albumin, globulin and AGR are as follows: albumin [area under the curve (AUC) 0.754, 95% CI: 0.671 – 0.838, cut-off value 3.35 g/dl], globulin (AUC 0.600, 95% CI: 0.507 – 0.692, cut-off value 3.85 g/dl), and AGR (AUC 0.769, 9",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n16",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Kaplan–Meier analysis of these two groups showed a significantly higher rate of lupus nephritis developing in the group with an AGR of < 0.807 (p < 0.001) (Fig. 2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n17",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Among the 391 Korean SLE patients, 99 patients had evident nephritis at initial presentation and 37 patients developed nephritis during follow up. Thus, the cumulative incidence of lupus nephritis was 34.8% (136 of 391)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n18",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The electronic medical records of patients who were diagnosed with SLE at a tertiary referral hospital in Seoul, South Korea between January 2005 and December 2015 were retrospectively reviewed.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n19",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "AGR was calculated using the equation AGR = albumin/(total protein − albumin).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n20",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Cox proportional hazard model was used to identify predictors of lupus nephritis. Univariate analysis was performed for each variable, and variables found to be statistically significant (p < 0.05) were included in multivariate analysis.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n21",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The proportional hazards assumption was confirmed by examination of log[−log(survival)] curves and by testing Schoenfeld partial residuals, and no relevant violations were found.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n22",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The discrimination ability of the multivariable model was evaluated using Harrell's overall c index.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n23",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Receiver operating characteristics (ROC) analysis was performed, and the best cut-off value was determined.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n24",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Survival rates were analysed using the Kaplan–Meier method and were compared using the log-rank test.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n25",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Kidney biopsy was performed according to ACR recommendations, including the following indications: increasing serum creatinine level of unknown cause or proteinuria ≥ 1 g per 24 h (either in a 24-h urine specimen or on a spot protein/creatinine ratio) or a",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n26",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "All patients met the American College of Rheumatology (ACR) classification criteria for SLE [13].",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n27",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The SLE Disease Activity Index, a validated measure of lupus disease activity [14], was assessed at the time SLE was diagnosed.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n28",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Predicting eventual development of lupus nephritis at the time of diagnosis of systemic lupus erythematosus",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n29",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Thus further studies are required with larger number of subjects from different ethnic populations to confirm the present results.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The electronic medical records of patients who were diagnosed with SLE at a tertiary referral hospital in Seoul, South Korea between January 2005 and December 2015 were retrospectively reviewed.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r19",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "In particular, a low AGR (aHR 4.972, 95% CI: 2.394 – 10.326, p < 0.001) was strongly associated with an increased risk of future lupus nephritis development.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r27",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "On multivariate analysis, the following factors remained significant: age [adjusted hazard ratio (aHR) 0.928, 95% confidence interval (CI): 0.895 – 0.961, p < 0.001], C3 (aHR 0.977, 95% CI: 0.966 – 0.989, p < 0.001), anti-dsDNA titre (aHR 1.004, 95% CI: 1.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r28",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "On multivariate analysis, the following factors remained significant: age [adjusted hazard ratio (aHR) 0.928, 95% confidence interval (CI): 0.895 – 0.961, p < 0.001], C3 (aHR 0.977, 95% CI: 0.966 – 0.989, p < 0.001), anti-dsDNA titre (aHR 1.004, 95% CI: 1.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r29",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Notably, the factor associated with the greatest hazard for lupus nephritis was a low AGR (aHR 4.972, 95% CI: 2.394 – 10.326, p < 0.001).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r30",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Based on the aHR, we estimated that risk of developing lupus nephritis increased by 4% per 100 IU/ml increase of anti-dsDNA titre.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r31",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The discrimination ability of the multivariable model was high (c index 0.898, 95% CI: 0.855 – 0.947).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r32",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "AGR, with the highest AUC, had the highest discrimination ability for development of lupus nephritis among the three variables.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r33",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Kaplan–Meier analysis of these two groups showed a significantly higher rate of lupus nephritis developing in the group with an AGR of < 0.807 (p < 0.001) (Fig. 2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r34",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Kaplan–Meier analysis of these two groups showed a significantly higher rate of lupus nephritis developing in the group with an AGR of < 0.807 (p < 0.001) (Fig. 2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r35",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Thus, the cumulative incidence of lupus nephritis was 34.8% (136 of 391)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r41",
