      ],
      "title": "Patients who developed nephritis were significantly younger at diagnosis (28.4 vs 40.8 years), had lower serum albumin (3.24 vs 3.86 g/dl), lower AGR (0.801 vs 1.044), lower C3 (55.8 vs 87.3 mg/dl), …",
      "content": "Patients who developed nephritis were significantly younger at diagnosis (28.4 vs 40.8 years), had lower serum albumin (3.24 vs 3.86 g/dl), lower AGR (0.801 vs 1.044), lower C3 (55.8 vs 87.3 mg/dl), lower C4 (9.2 vs 15.8 mg/dl), higher anti-dsDNA titre (97.0 vs 8.1 IU/ml), higher SLEDAI (13.0 vs 8.2), higher frequency of anti-Sm (31.3% vs 13.8%), anti-RNP (54.1% vs 28.7%), and anti-beta2 glycoprotein IgM (16.7% vs 5.6%), and received higher cumulative glucocorticoid dose.",
      "created": "2026-11-06T16:31:32.561Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T16:31:32.561Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n11",
